<Task version="1.4" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/windows/2004/02/mit/task">
  <RegistrationInfo>
    <Author>Gamma_X</Author>
    <Description>Generates the GEX dashboard and publishes it to the snapshot branch that GitHub Pages serves. Every 15 minutes through the evening session, 18:20 to 02:45, Sunday evening to Friday morning, around the main task's 18:20, 20:00 and 00:00. Runs only push when the figures actually change (--skip-unchanged). All times are the machine's local clock, so set it to Eastern. Each occurrence is its own trigger, generated by tools/make_schedule.py - WakeToRun wakes the PC for a trigger's START BOUNDARY and never for a repetition inside a trigger's duration, so the repetitions this used to use were lost on a sleeping machine: 3 of 3 start boundaries fired unattended over 09-21 to 09-23, and 0 of 141 repetitions did. The day is split across two tasks because Task Scheduler rejects a document with more than 48 triggers and the full schedule is 48, at the limit. publish_snapshot.bat also holds the machine awake across the session by setting both sleep timers, the attended idle one and the unattended one whose 120s default was returning the PC to sleep after each run. Either mechanism alone is enough; both are in place because this failed twice.</Description>
    <URI>\Gamma_X Snapshot Evening</URI>
  </RegistrationInfo>
  <Triggers>
